-- title:
--   From HTo G Averaged Eligible Sandwich Total Eq Type Sum
-- statement:
--   **The averaged eligible sandwich total is the sum of eligible per-type totals.**
--
--   Let `params` have a field model, let `family` be an indexed polynomial submeasurement family, and let `k` be a natural number. The total of `averagedEligibleSandwichSubMeas`, obtained by uniformly averaging the interpolation-eligible sandwich family over point tuples, satisfies
--
--   $$
--   \bigl(\operatorname{averagedEligibleSandwichSubMeas}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},k)\bigr).\operatorname{total}
--   =
--   \sum_{\tau\in\{0,1\}^{k}}
--   \begin{cases}
--   \bigl(\operatorname{averagedSandwichByTypeSubMeas}(\mathrm{params},\mathrm{family},k,\tau)\bigr).\operatorname{total},
--   &d+1\le |\tau|,\\
--   0,&d+1>|\tau|.
--   \end{cases}
--   $$
--
--   The identity first applies the pointwise type partition and then exchanges the finite type sum with the uniform average. It is the stage-zero bookkeeping input to `fromHToGStageMass_zero_eq`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_averagedEligibleSandwich_total_eq_type_sum`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
